{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design", "label": "M3e Video Extras Design", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_server_timing", "label": "Server-authoritative video timing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "decision 1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If the client delayed its own state locally, headless users would measure undelayed signals - the sim's data would disagree with the pilot's experience, and drops would be invisible to tests, logs and determinism."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_field_drops", "label": "Field drops confined to the marginal SNR band", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "2, decision 5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A locked link never drops fields and a lost link is already static - drops outside the band would be invisible or wrong; a dropped field never updates the SyncTracker."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_render_instant", "label": "Delayed field-quantized render instant (sim_now - latency)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pose, video quality and OSD all sample one shared field-quantized instant, so the picture ages as a unit at 50 Hz (the analog judder) and no layer can disagree about when it is."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_subviewport", "label": "FPV composite as a SubViewport (DVR + aspect seam)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "4, decision 4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capturing a window region would include the HUD and re-implement the boxing per layer; the SubViewport at a fixed internal resolution is what makes DVR honest and what the aspect setting sizes."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_dvr_degraded", "label": "DVR records the degraded composite the pilot sees", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "decision 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What real goggle DVR captures is the degraded link; a clean recording is a different feature."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_avi_muxer", "label": "Own MJPEG AVI muxer in ofs-client (no external dependency)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "5, decision 3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An image sequence plus manual ffmpeg gives a folder, not a file; piping to ffmpeg needs an external binary; JPEG comes from Godot's built-in encoder."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_tramp", "label": "Tramp codec behind the existing VtxModel ([vtx] kind)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The codec owns the wire (framing, CRC, commands); the model keeps its shared state; Tramp's quirks live inside the codec - power in mW natively, pit mode as its own command, frequency set directly in MHz."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_font_page1", "label": "OSD font page 1 drawn from stacked atlas pages", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The server already decodes the DisplayPort attribute bits into cells (ch | page << 8 | blink << 10); pages stack vertically in the atlas; pages beyond what is shipped draw from page 0 defensively."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_aspect", "label": "Aspect setting (4:3 default, 16:9, window)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "4:3 is the goggles-honest shape; it sizes the SubViewport and the OSD fills it naturally, replacing M3a's OSD-only box logic in a better shape."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_protocol_7", "label": "Protocol 7 (VideoLink.field_valid, latency_ms)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3c_world_collision_elrs_design", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "header (predecessor whose milestone table created this one)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3d_fc_telemetry_design", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "header (builds on M3d's merged output, protocol 6)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_04_open_fpv_sim_design", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "header (parent spec)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_server_timing", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_render_instant", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "decision 1 -> 3 (server models latency/drops; client composites from delayed samples)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_subviewport", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_avi_muxer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "decision 4 (the SubViewport is what makes DVR honest)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_dvr_degraded", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_avi_muxer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "decision 2 -> 5 (record exactly what the pilot sees)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_render_instant", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_field_drops", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "3 (a dropped field holds the previous composite)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_field_drops", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_09_m3b_video_link_design_sync_thresholds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "2 (drop band uses M3b's UNSTABLE_SNR_DB / LOST_SNR_DB)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_tramp", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_08_m3a_osd_vtx_design_vtx_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "6 (behind the existing VtxModel, selected by the [vtx] kind field M3a reserved)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_font_page1", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_08_m3a_osd_vtx_design_font_atlas", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "4 (make_osd_font.py grows a second .mcm argument, pages stack vertically)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_10_m3e_video_extras_design_aspect", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_08_m3a_osd_vtx_design", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-10-m3e-video-extras-design.md", "source_location": "4 